# Optional: point the app at your own TURN server.
#
# WebRTC needs a TURN relay to connect players whose networks use
# symmetric NAT or block UDP (common on public / café Wi-Fi). If these
# variables are left unset, the app uses the Open Relay Project's free
# public TURN servers — fine for trying things out, but a shared free
# service is best-effort.
#
# For a dependable relay, create a free TURN server (e.g. a free Metered
# account at https://www.metered.ca/ , or self-host coturn) and set:
#
#   VITE_TURN_URLS        Comma-separated TURN URLs. Include a TCP/443
#                         (turns:) entry so it works where UDP is blocked.
#   VITE_TURN_USERNAME    TURN username.
#   VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL  TURN credential / password.
#
# To use these in the GitHub Pages deploy, add them as repository
# secrets and pass them to the build step in .github/workflows/deploy.yml.

# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:your.turn.host:3478,turns:your.turn.host:443?transport=tcp
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=your-username
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-credential
